Neon spaces (M2), part 5 of 5: commands.

Next space (Ctrl+Alt+Down), previous space (Ctrl+Alt+Up) and space 1..9
(Alt+Shift+1..9) on Linux and Windows, dispatched to neon::spaces from
BrowserCommandController, with labels for Helium's shortcuts settings page so
they can be rebound. The command ids live in Neon's own header, not
chrome_command_ids.h. macOS defaults wait for Mac access (M6).

